WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:17.940
Claw enables rich VR interactions in a
compact, handheld free-moving device.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:25.460
With claw you can grasp ritual objects and
feel appropriate forces during grasping.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:32.820
You can also touch and feel the shape of
a virtual object as well as get

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:38.370
resistance when you push on them.
You can also rub virtual surfaces and

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:44.309
feel their texture rendered underneath
your fingertip. Finally, you can also feel

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:50.819
the recoil when shooting the virtual
weapon. Claw is a unique, multi-functional

00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:55.879
haptic controller that enables grasping,

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:59.160
touching,

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:06.379
surface texture rendering,
and shooting feedback.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.720
By reading the thumb position using a 
proximity sensor

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:16.280
our controller changes its haptic mode
between grasping and touching

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.330
We use a force center located at the
fingertip mount to enable closed loop

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:27.420
force feedback control system with a
servo motor.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:37.340
The servo motor only reacts
to the forces exerted by the index finger.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:42.780
With the closed loop force control
we can render variable stiffness.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.460
For example, users can grab and feel

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:52.700
solid virtual objects but also soft
deformable virtual objects.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:58.660
A voice coil actuator at the fingertip generates
different patterns of vibration which

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:02.400
are used for texture rendering.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:10.220
Coupled with the 3D hand tracking data
the voice coil actuator vibrates only

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:14.780
when the user moves their hand. When
shooting, the servo motor moves back and

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:24.580
forth quickly to simulate recoil
sensation.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:32.860
In summary, the clock controller integrates multiple haptic technologies into a VR controller device

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:37.960
capable of rendering compelling force
feedback while grasping, touching,

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:41.380
and shooting in virtual reality.

